	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey">
		<text>Survey</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_desc">
		<text>Ask a scientific network, from an artifact's entry, where one could be. Word comes later as a PDA message: a level, never a spot, good until the next emission or psi storm.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_network">
		<text>Survey: whose network</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_network_desc">
		<text>Whose standing buys the survey. With Seasons of the Zone, its forecast's network is used instead, so one standing buys both. The best of the three goes by whoever thinks most of you.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="almanac_survey_network_lst_ecolog">
		<text>Ecologists</text>
	</string>
	<string id="almanac_survey_network_lst_csky">
		<text>Clear Sky</text>
	</string>
	<string id="almanac_survey_network_lst_isg">
		<text>ISG</text>
	</string>
	<string id="almanac_survey_network_lst_best">
		<text>The best of the three</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_could">
		<text>Survey: standing for word that one could turn up</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_could_desc">
		<text>From this standing the network names a level its next roll could make one on. The nearer the next step, the likelier the level it names.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_is">
		<text>Survey: standing for word that one is there</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_is_desc">
		<text>From this standing the network also says where one lies free now, or else names the likeliest level and its odds.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_per_day">
		<text>Survey: questions a day</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_per_day_desc">
		<text>How many questions the network answers each game day.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_wait_min">
		<text>Survey: shortest wait for word (game minutes)</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_wait_min_desc">
		<text>The game clock runs six times real time: 60 game minutes are 10 real ones.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_wait_max">
		<text>Survey: longest wait for word (game minutes)</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_almanac_survey_wait_max_desc">
		<text>Word comes at a random time between the shortest and the longest wait, and waits for an emission or psi storm to pass.</text>
	</string>
